  "id": "bas",
  "term": "BAS",
  "definition": "BAS is a smoking-cessation program that aims to keep a person’s sense of reward and reinforcement up after quitting. It does this by increasing rewarding non-smoking activities and reducing dependence on food as a replacement for smoking, which may help lower weight-related relapse risk.",
